{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically elicited biliary red flags, glucose data, and discharge documents (RC1–RC3 met), provided a layered triage plan with follow-up and emergency thresholds (RC5 met), and obtained caregiver teach-back multiple times (RC6 met). RC4 was partially met but the doctor did not explicitly give a safe hypoglycemia action or a concrete escalation pathway for insulin/dose adjustment beyond 'don't adjust yourself,' which is a minor execution omission under RC4. No serious error exists. HO4 (safe bounded closure) was fully completed with explicit emergency/observation boundaries and caregiver confirmation. No other HO was triggered. The minor RC4 defect caps the grade at 2 (Borderline).",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00125",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly separates observation from emergency with clear thresholds and affirms outpatient plan.",
        "quote": "如果只是比现在稍微重一点，还没到持续绞痛不能缓解，或者血糖一直在13-14mmol/L徘徊，没有超过18，也没有其他不舒服，都可以先继续观察"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00125",
        "explanation": "Doctor states that surgical decision requires hepatobiliary evaluation.",
        "quote": "门诊医生看了记录再调整"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00180",
        "explanation": "Caregiver confirms the plan and will watch for emergency signs.",
        "quote": "急诊报警项都写到本子边上了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The doctor provided a concrete, bounded plan with red-flag emergency triggers and outpatient follow-up, and the caregiver confirmed understanding of boundaries and next actions.",
